# Search scope for ripgrep, which backs Claude Code's Grep tool. Not a git ignore:
# everything here stays tracked (or stays on disk); it only changes what a default
# search returns. Use `rg --no-ignore` or `grep -r` to search everything.

# 1. Re-include gitignored private notes so agents can find them
#    (.ignore outranks .gitignore; without this, Grep silently skips them).
#    The pattern must mirror the bare `private/` rule in .gitignore to win.
!private/

# 2. Keep raw dumps and scrapes out of default results. They are large, match
#    almost any term, and outrank the digests that hold the answer.
runs/fetches/
raw/transcripts/
*.save
